<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S3.F4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">NCM’s two-stage training.<span id="S3.F4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> </span>(a)<span id="S3.F4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A multiscale residual VQ-VAE learns to encode text into a coarse-to-fine hierarchy of discrete codes <math id="S3.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},\ldots,r_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},\ldots,r_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and reconstruct the input. </span>(b)<span id="S3.F4.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The </span>NCM<span id="S3.F4.8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> transformer predicts all codes within level <math id="S3.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in parallel from the cumulative reconstruction <math id="S3.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, resized to <math id="S3.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> positions. In the unconditional setting, block-diagonal attention restricts each input block to itself. During training, all <math id="S3.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> levels are predicted in one forward pass using a cross-entropy loss. During generation, levels are predicted sequentially from coarse to fine.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given latent vectors <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and a codebook
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{|\mathcal{V}|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{|\mathcal{V}|}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, with entries
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">vector quantization</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>
replaces each vector <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with its nearest codebook entry:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{q}^{i}=\arg\min_{e\in\mathcal{V}}\|z^{i}-e\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{q}^{i}=\arg\min_{e\in\mathcal{V}}\|z^{i}-e\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The selected codebook vectors form the quantized latent
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A single quantization step generally leaves an approximation error. <em id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Residual
quantization</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> represents this error using
additional codebooks, adding each quantized correction to the reconstruction.
Starting from the residual <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(0)}=z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(0)}=z</annotation></semantics></math>
and the reconstruction <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(0)}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(0)}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(k),i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(k),i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the residual
vector at position <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> after level <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k),i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k),i}</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding
cumulative reconstruction vector. Level <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> quantizes the residual into
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> codes <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and updates the reconstruction and residual. Here <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(r_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(r_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>
denotes lookup in level <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>’s codebook, with <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(r_{k})^{i}=e_{k,r_{k}^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(r_{k})^{i}=e_{k,r_{k}^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}=\hat{z}^{(k-1)}+e_{k}(r_{k}),\qquad z^{(k)}=z-\hat{z}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}=\hat{z}^{(k-1)}+e_{k}(r_{k}),\qquad z^{(k)}=z-\hat{z}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The sum <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(K)}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}e_{k}(r_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(K)}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}e_{k}(r_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> approximates <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, and each partial sum
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="S3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cumulative reconstruction</em>, is a partial reconstruction
using the first <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> levels.
<em id="S3.SS1.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Multiscale residual quantization</em>
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> uses progressively longer code sequences, with
level <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> codes. Its codebook vectors are mapped to a
length-<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> contribution by a reconstruction operator <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> before being added
to the cumulative reconstruction, allowing
shorter, coarse levels to be followed by finer levels that add detail.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Formulation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{T}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{T}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens from a text vocabulary <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The tokenizer maps <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to discrete codes at <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> levels,</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{1:K}=(r_{1},\ldots,r_{K}),\qquad r_{k}\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{V}_{k}|\}^{\ell_{k}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1:K}=(r_{1},\ldots,r_{K}),\qquad r_{k}\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{V}_{k}|\}^{\ell_{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is level <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>’s codebook, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> is its size,
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of codes at that level, and
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}&lt;\ell_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;\ell_{K}=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}&lt;\ell_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;\ell_{K}=L</annotation></semantics></math>. Each level encodes the residual left
by the earlier ones. The generator predicts the levels from coarse to fine,
conditioning on earlier levels through their cumulative reconstruction
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p_{\theta}(r_{k}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p_{\theta}(r_{k}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Conditional on this reconstruction, the codes within each
level are sampled independently, allowing all positions to be generated in
one forward pass:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(r_{k}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)})=\prod_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}p_{\theta}(r_{k}^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(r_{k}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)})=\prod_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}p_{\theta}(r_{k}^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">After all levels are generated, the tokenizer’s decoder maps their cumulative
reconstruction <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(K)}</annotation></semantics></math> to token distributions at all <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> positions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Multiscale Residual Tokenization</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain the hierarchy, we learn a multiscale residual VQ-VAE, using nested
dropout to encourage informative partial reconstructions.
An encoder <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the input sequence <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> latent vectors of
dimension <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=E_{\phi}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=E_{\phi}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Starting from <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(0)}=z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(0)}=z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(0)}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(0)}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, each level quantizes the residual left by the preceding levels. At level <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the residual is downsampled to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> latent vectors, and each vector is assigned the index of its nearest entry in the codebook <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}=\mathrm{Down}_{k}(z^{(k-1)})\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell_{k}\times d},\qquad r_{k}^{i}=\arg\min_{j\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{V}_{k}|\}}\|u_{k}^{i}-e_{k,j}\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Down</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}=\mathrm{Down}_{k}(z^{(k-1)})\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell_{k}\times d},\qquad r_{k}^{i}=\arg\min_{j\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{V}_{k}|\}}\|u_{k}^{i}-e_{k,j}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The reconstruction operator <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the selected codebook vectors to a
length-<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> contribution, which we add to the cumulative reconstruction:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}=\hat{z}^{(k-1)}+R_{k}(e_{k}(r_{k})),\qquad z^{(k)}=z-\hat{z}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}=\hat{z}^{(k-1)}+R_{k}(e_{k}(r_{k})),\qquad z^{(k)}=z-\hat{z}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}(r_{k})\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell_{k}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}(r_{k})\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell_{k}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the selected codebook
vectors, and both <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> have shape <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\times d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The VQ-VAE decoder defines token distributions
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\psi}(x^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\psi}(x^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> at all <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> positions from a cumulative
reconstruction <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Nested dropout.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use nested dropout
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, which during training retains only the first <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> levels for a sampled
cutoff <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\ldots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\ldots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}=\sum_{j=1}^{k}R_{j}(e_{j}(r_{j}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}=\sum_{j=1}^{k}R_{j}(e_{j}(r_{j}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
This encourages earlier levels to capture meaningful information rather than
relying on finer levels to carry it.
During training, both the reconstruction cross-entropy
and the VQ terms are evaluated at the sampled cutoff:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{tok}}=-\frac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\log p_{\psi}(x^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k)})+\beta\,\mathrm{MSE}\!\left(z,\mathrm{sg}[\hat{z}^{(k)}]\right)+\mathrm{MSE}\!\left(\mathrm{sg}[z],\hat{z}^{(k)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>tok</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mpadded style="width:2.376em;" width="2.376em"><mi>MSE</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>sg</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mpadded style="width:2.376em;" width="2.376em"><mi>MSE</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>sg</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{tok}}=-\frac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\log p_{\psi}(x^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k)})+\beta\,\mathrm{MSE}\!\left(z,\mathrm{sg}[\hat{z}^{(k)}]\right)+\mathrm{MSE}\!\left(\mathrm{sg}[z],\hat{z}^{(k)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The VQ terms combine a commitment loss and a latent quantization loss, both
measured by mean squared error (MSE).
Here <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>sg</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sg}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes stop-gradient and
<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> weights the commitment term.
We use a straight-through estimator to pass reconstruction gradients through
the discrete quantization step to the encoder.</p>
</div>
