<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Coarse-to-Fine Generation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the tokenizer frozen, we train the <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> transformer on all levels in one forward pass (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Conditioning Corruption. ‣ 3.4 Coarse-to-Fine Generation ‣ 3 Next-Concept Modeling ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>); generation proceeds from coarse to fine in <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> steps (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Conditioning Corruption. ‣ 3.4 Coarse-to-Fine Generation ‣ 3 Next-Concept Modeling ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conditioning Corruption.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To improve robustness to accumulating VQ code errors during generation, we train with a fraction of conditioning codes replaced by other codes from the same level’s codebook, keeping the ground-truth codes intact as labels. Replacement probabilities vary by level; ablations are given in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Code Corruption ‣ Appendix F Ablations ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>. Let <math id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}^{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}^{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the resulting cumulative reconstruction. The training objective is</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NCM}}=-\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}\sum_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}\log p_{\theta}(r_{k}^{i}\mid\tilde{z}^{(k-1)}),\qquad w_{k}=\frac{\ell_{k}^{-\alpha}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\ell_{j}^{1-\alpha}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>NCM</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NCM}}=-\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}\sum_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}\log p_{\theta}(r_{k}^{i}\mid\tilde{z}^{(k-1)}),\qquad w_{k}=\frac{\ell_{k}^{-\alpha}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\ell_{j}^{1-\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, all code positions have equal weight, and with <math id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, each level has equal weight.</p>
</div>
