<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Probabilistic Formulation and ELBO</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formulate <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> as a hierarchical latent-variable model and derive an evidence
lower bound (ELBO) on its text log-likelihood. We consider unconditional generation
with deterministic nearest-neighbor code assignments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Next-Concept Modeling ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{T}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{T}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens
from the text vocabulary <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The tokenizer assigns <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> a hierarchy
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{*}_{1:K}(x)=(r^{*}_{1},\ldots,r^{*}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}_{1:K}(x)=(r^{*}_{1},\ldots,r^{*}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}^{*}\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{V}_{k}|\}^{\ell_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}^{*}\in\{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{V}_{k}|\}^{\ell_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\ell_{K}=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\ell_{K}=L</annotation></semantics></math>. We fix the tokenizer’s parameters and use a fixed
rule to break nearest-neighbor ties, so this assignment is deterministic.
For any code hierarchy <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{1:K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1:K}</annotation></semantics></math>, define its cumulative reconstruction by</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}(r_{1:k})=\sum_{j=1}^{k}R_{j}\bigl(e_{j}(r_{j})\bigr),\qquad\hat{z}^{(0)}=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}(r_{1:k})=\sum_{j=1}^{k}R_{j}\bigl(e_{j}(r_{j})\bigr),\qquad\hat{z}^{(0)}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the codebook lookup and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reconstruction operator
of Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Multiscale Residual Tokenization ‣ 3 Next-Concept Modeling ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.
The decoder defines a likelihood over text,</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})=\prod_{n=1}^{L}p_{\psi}\bigl(x^{n}\mid\hat{z}^{(K)}(r_{1:K})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})=\prod_{n=1}^{L}p_{\psi}\bigl(x^{n}\mid\hat{z}^{(K)}(r_{1:K})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the generator defines a prior over hierarchies,</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p_{\theta}\bigl(r_{k}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)}\bigr)=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\prod_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}p_{\theta}\bigl(r_{k}^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})=\prod_{k=1}^{K}p_{\theta}\bigl(r_{k}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)}\bigr)=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\prod_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}p_{\theta}\bigl(r_{k}^{i}\mid\hat{z}^{(k-1)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k-1)}=\hat{z}^{(k-1)}(r_{1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k-1)}=\hat{z}^{(k-1)}(r_{1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Each factor is normalized
for every preceding hierarchy, so their product defines a normalized prior.
The joint distribution and marginal text likelihood are</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta,\psi}(x,r_{1:K})=p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})p_{\theta}(r_{1:K}),\qquad p_{\theta,\psi}(x)=\sum_{r_{1:K}}p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta,\psi}(x,r_{1:K})=p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})p_{\theta}(r_{1:K}),\qquad p_{\theta,\psi}(x)=\sum_{r_{1:K}}p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})p_{\theta}(r_{1:K}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
