<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Evidence Lower Bound</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Use the tokenizer’s deterministic assignment as a point-mass variational distribution,</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(r_{1:K}\mid x)=\mathbf{1}\{r_{1:K}=r^{*}_{1:K}(x)\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(r_{1:K}\mid x)=\mathbf{1}\{r_{1:K}=r^{*}_{1:K}(x)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This distribution has zero entropy. Its ELBO therefore reduces to the log joint
probability of the tokenizer’s assigned hierarchy:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv\mathbb{E}_{q(r_{1:K}\mid x)}\left[\log p_{\theta,\psi}(x,r_{1:K})-\log q(r_{1:K}\mid x)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv\mathbb{E}_{q(r_{1:K}\mid x)}\left[\log p_{\theta,\psi}(x,r_{1:K})-\log q(r_{1:K}\mid x)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\psi}(x\mid r^{*}_{1:K})+\log p_{\theta}(r^{*}_{1:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\psi}(x\mid r^{*}_{1:K})+\log p_{\theta}(r^{*}_{1:K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\sum_{r_{1:K}}p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})=\log p_{\theta,\psi}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\sum_{r_{1:K}}p_{\psi}(x\mid r_{1:K})p_{\theta}(r_{1:K})=\log p_{\theta,\psi}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The inequality follows because the marginal likelihood sums nonnegative terms and
includes the term for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{*}_{1:K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}_{1:K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{z}_{*}^{(k)}=\hat{z}^{(k)}(r^{*}_{1:k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{*}^{(k)}=\hat{z}^{(k)}(r^{*}_{1:k})</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting
(<a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ A.1 Setup ‣ Appendix A Probabilistic Formulation and ELBO ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ A.1 Setup ‣ Appendix A Probabilistic Formulation and ELBO ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}(x)=\underbrace{\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log p_{\psi}\bigl(x^{n}\mid\hat{z}_{*}^{(K)}\bigr)}_{\text{reconstruction}}+\underbrace{\sum_{k=1}^{K}\sum_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}\log p_{\theta}\bigl(r_{k}^{*i}\mid\hat{z}_{*}^{(k-1)}\bigr)}_{\text{generation}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>reconstruction</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>generation</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}(x)=\underbrace{\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log p_{\psi}\bigl(x^{n}\mid\hat{z}_{*}^{(K)}\bigr)}_{\text{reconstruction}}+\underbrace{\sum_{k=1}^{K}\sum_{i=1}^{\ell_{k}}\log p_{\theta}\bigl(r_{k}^{*i}\mid\hat{z}_{*}^{(k-1)}\bigr)}_{\text{generation}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}^{*i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}^{*i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th code at level <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the assigned hierarchy.
The gap to the log-likelihood is exactly</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{\theta,\psi}(x)-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{\theta,\psi}(x)-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(r_{1:K}\mid x)\,\|\,p_{\theta,\psi}(r_{1:K}\mid x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(r_{1:K}\mid x)\,\|\,p_{\theta,\psi}(r_{1:K}\mid x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta,\psi}(r^{*}_{1:K}\mid x)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta,\psi}(r^{*}_{1:K}\mid x)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Thus, the bound is tight if and only if the posterior assigns probability one to
the tokenizer’s hierarchy. With finite softmax logits, the prior and decoder assign
positive probability to every hierarchy and text sequence, so the bound and gap
are finite.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a frozen tokenizer and decoder, only the generation term depends on <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
With clean conditioning and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the generator loss in
Section <a href="#S3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="Conditioning Corruption. ‣ 3.4 Coarse-to-Fine Generation ‣ 3 Next-Concept Modeling ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> is the negative generation term divided by the total
number of codes <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>; minimizing it therefore maximizes this
ELBO over <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditioning corruption and nonuniform level weighting modify
that objective. The bound uses the complete hierarchy; nested dropout and the
quantization losses used to train the tokenizer are not included in it.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Datasets</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train a separate tokenizer and generator for each of six datasets, grouped by task
as in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Datasets ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes them.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T4.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T4.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.45pt 3.5pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T4.3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Dataset</span></span>
