<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Architecture Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A tokenizer and a generator are trained for each dataset (Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Datasets ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>):
the tokenizer first, and it is then frozen as the generator trains. For XSum and WMT14,
the generator is initially trained with unpaired text, then with source–target pairs.
The target length schedule and level schedule remain unchanged.
Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.1 Multiscale VQVAE Tokenizer ‣ Appendix C Architecture Details ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> describes the tokenizers’ architectures and training.
Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ C.2 Generator (NCM) ‣ Appendix C Architecture Details ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> provides details about the generators’ architectures,
training, and sampling. The datasets are listed in the same order as in
Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Tokenizer Quality ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. All experiments employed seed 42, BF16 mixed-precision and
<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch.compile</span>.</p>
</div>
