<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training-token accounting.</span>
Budgets count full-length text positions, including padding and repeated data exposure.
For LM1B, tokenizer and generator training total
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25{,}957\times 2{,}048\times 128+100{,}000\times 512\times 128\approx 13.36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>25,957</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2,048</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100,000</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>512</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>13.36</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25{,}957\times 2{,}048\times 128+100{,}000\times 512\times 128\approx 13.36</annotation></semantics></math>B positions (<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6.80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.80</annotation></semantics></math>B+<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.55</annotation></semantics></math>B).
For OpenWebText, the corresponding total is
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="78{,}432\times 768\times 1{,}024+250{,}000\times 256\times 1{,}024\approx 127.22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>78,432</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>768</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1,024</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>250,000</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1,024</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>127.22</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">78{,}432\times 768\times 1{,}024+250{,}000\times 256\times 1{,}024\approx 127.22</annotation></semantics></math>B positions (<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="61.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>61.68</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">61.68</annotation></semantics></math>B+<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="65.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>65.54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">65.54</annotation></semantics></math>B), approximately <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> fewer than
the <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math>B-plus tokens used by MDLM and DUO
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.
Scaling plots exclude the shared tokenizer. These budgets measure token exposure, not FLOPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each generator block contains self-attention followed by a feed-forward layer.
The resized reconstruction <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and prompt embeddings are projected to
the hidden width before the first block. Attention heads have dimension <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math>,
equal to the hidden width divided by the number of heads.</p>
</div>
