<section id="A6.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.2 </span>Context Encoder</h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To support conditional generation, <span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> uses a prefix LM. One design decision is
how to encode the prefix. On XSum, we compare the frozen encoder from pretrained
T5-small with the encoder from our VQ-VAE (Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.2.2 Context Encoder ‣ F.2 NCM Transformer ‣ Appendix F Ablations ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>). T5-small
achieves slightly higher ROUGE scores: <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.10</annotation></semantics></math> ROUGE-1, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.15</annotation></semantics></math> ROUGE-2, and
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.24</annotation></semantics></math> ROUGE-L. However, it adds <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="35.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>35.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">35.3</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters, approximately a <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40\%</annotation></semantics></math>
increase over our <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="88" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>88</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">88</annotation></semantics></math>M model, and introduces a dependency on an externally
pretrained language model. We therefore use the encoder from our VQ-VAE in all
reported experiments.</p>
</div>
