<section id="A6.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.3 </span>Loss Weighting</h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The loss weights level <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}\propto\ell_{k}^{-\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\propto\ell_{k}^{-\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math> weights every code
equally, as the ELBO does (Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Evidence Lower Bound ‣ Appendix A Probabilistic Formulation and ELBO ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>), and <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> every level
equally. On TinyStories (setup of Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Code Corruption ‣ Appendix F Ablations ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>), raising <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math> moves the coarse levels’ share of the loss from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>19</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="63\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>63</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">63\%</annotation></semantics></math> and lowers their
validation loss, yet Gen. PPL after <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>k steps stays at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>18.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18.9</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>19.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19.0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>
and rises slightly to <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>19.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19.4</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math> (Figure <a href="#A6.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ F.2.3 Loss Weighting ‣ F.2 NCM Transformer ‣ Appendix F Ablations ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</p>
