<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reconstruction &amp; Utilization.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A7.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ Reconstruction &amp; Utilization. ‣ Appendix G Tokenizer Analysis ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> shows how the reconstruction builds up across the
hierarchy of the OpenWebText (OWT) tokenizer. After each level <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we decode the cumulative reconstruction <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>
and measure exact token accuracy on held-out data. We also report the fraction of each
level’s codebook entries used and its effective codebook utilization, measured by
codebook perplexity. Reconstruction accuracy increases across levels, reaching
<math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99.99\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>99.99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99.99\%</annotation></semantics></math> at full resolution.</p>
