<div id="A8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Perturbing Early Codes.</span>
We perturb a story’s coarse representation by replacing two codes with random
codes observed at the same level across validation stories, then generate the
finer levels. Using the same sampling seed, we compare outputs with and without
these replacements. Figure <a href="#A8.F19" title="Figure 19 ‣ Appendix H Probing the Hierarchy ‣ N C M Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> shows that changing two
coarse codes can alter characters, objects, and events while preserving parts of
the narrative.</p>
