<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Limitations &amp; Future Work</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> shows promising results on unconditional generation and downstream conditional
generation tasks such as summarization and translation. Several directions remain for
further improvement. <span id="A9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> fixes both the hierarchy depth <math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and the per-level lengths
<math id="A9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so even short continuations traverse the full hierarchy; an input-dependent
schedule would adapt compute to example complexity. <span id="A9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> relies on a separately
trained multiscale VQ-VAE tokenizer, decoupling representation learning from the
generative objective. An end-to-end training approach could benefit <span id="A9.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span> by aligning
representation learning with the generative objective. Our main experiments use generators of roughly <math id="A9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>M
parameters, and our scaling study extends to <math id="A9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="725" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>725</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">725</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters on LM1B. Scaling to
larger datasets and model sizes is another exciting direction. Generations are
generally fluent but exhibit occasional artifacts at coarse-level transitions,
presenting another opportunity to further improve <span id="A9.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NCM</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
